Z||000000||speed racer||12-25-2000||11:16 PM||||The Maga-White lite kit form the Fiero Store.<BR>And how do you like them ||||reg||1
Z||000001||80's BOY||12-25-2000||11:28 PM||||i bought that kit last year. i think it was fairly inexpensive, like 70 bucks or something. i got the gold colored bulbs not white. here's how i rate it:<P>1) craftsmanship= sloppy<P>the lenses are plastic, and siliconed with obvious finger smears in the corners for uniformity on the rear of them. looks like someone thought up the idea and built it....without professional help.<P>2) streetability= superb!<P>the lights i have are excellent for driving, and are far superior to a stock headlight.<P>3) cost= reasonable<P>considering a regular set of ion hyperwhite bulbs will cost in the 40 - 60 dollar range...for the bulbs only mind you...makes this kit very reasonable. it includes the replacement lense housing, acting as a total headlight replacement, along with rubber seals and spring catches to hold in the bulbs.<P>there you have it. keep in mind that my car never sees the rain, and is a weekend cruiser. very low hours on my lights so far. also, i live in south texas so no extreme cold temps here either. would i buy them again?? yes. do i recommend them?? yes. i simply thought they could have been put more engineering into the design before selling them in mass quantities. hope this helps.<P>Brian O<BR>||||reg||6
